54:- empty — covered: empty wrap input, empty diff inputs, empty pad input, and an empty template.
55:- singleton — covered: single-line wrap and one-line diff inputs.
58:- type_mismatch — covered: `text.wrap(1, 5)`, `text.diff("a", 1)`, `text.dedent(1)`, `text.template("<<name>>", 1)`, a non-numeric width and a non-text fill all produce catchable errors naming the operation on both engines.
60:- unicode — covered: `pad`, `align` and `wrap` use character counts for `é` and CJK text, where bytes differ; a CJK word longer than the width is split by characters, and a non-ASCII fill repeats by character.
64:- resource_limit — covered: `wrap`/`pad`/`align` cap the width at 1,000,000 characters, `pad`/`align` reserve their output with `try_reserve_exact` bounded by the widest emitted character rather than the whole fill, and `diff` refuses a line table past 4,000,000 cells. Each refusal is a catchable `RuntimeError` naming the operation; `wrap` also no longer recounts the current line for every word.
